{"id":8196961,"docketId":65294768,"caseName":"Ex parte Abernathy","caseNameFull":"EX PARTE ABERNATHY","slug":"ex-parte-abernathy","docketNumber":"","dateFiled":"1943-10-18","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1943,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":null,"natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":35,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8158896,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":3106,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<author id=\"b285-12\">Per Curiam.</author>\n<p id=\"b285-13\">The applications are severally denied.</p>\n<p id=\"b285-14\">In these cases petitioners invoke the exercise of the jurisdiction conferred on this Court by <span class=\"citation no-link\">28 U. S. C. \u00a7\u00a7 377</span>, <page-number citation-index=\"1\" label=\"220\">*220</page-number>451, to issue writs of habeas corpus in aid of its appellate jurisdiction. Cf. <em>Ex parte Peru, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9419326\"><a href=\"/opinion/103805/ex-parte-republic-of-peru/#582\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ex Parte Republic of Peru\">318 U. S. 578, 582-3</a></span>. That jurisdiction is discretionary, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9419326\"><a href=\"/opinion/103805/ex-parte-republic-of-peru/#584\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ex Parte Republic of Peru\"><em>id. </em>584</a></span>; <em>Bowen </em>v. <em>Johnston, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"103134\"><a href=\"/opinion/103134/bowen-v-johnston/#27\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Bowen v. Johnston\">306 U. S. 19, 27</a></span>, and this Court does not, save in exceptional circumstances, exercise it in cases where an adequate remedy may be had in a lower federal court, <em>Ex parte Current, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"8156726\"><a href=\"/opinion/8194791/ex-parte-current/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ex parte Current\">314 U. S. 578</a></span>; <em>Ex parte Spaulding, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"8157838\"><a href=\"/opinion/8195903/ex-parte-spaulding/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ex parte Spaulding\">317 U. S. 593</a></span>; <em>Ex parte Hawk, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"8158375\"><a href=\"/opinion/8196440/ex-parte-hawk/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ex parte Hawk\">318 U. S. 746</a></span>, or, if the relief sought is from the judgment of a state court, where the petitioner has not exhausted his remedies in the state courts, <em>Mooney </em>v. <em>Holohan, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"102372\"><a href=\"/opinion/102372/mooney-v-holohan/#115\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Mooney v. Holohan\">294 U. S. 103, 115</a></span>; <em>Ex parte Botwinski, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"8156760\"><a href=\"/opinion/8194825/ex-parte-botwinski/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ex parte Botwinski\">314 U. S. 586</a></span>; <em>Ex parte Davis, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"8157833\"><a href=\"/opinion/8195898/ex-parte-davis/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ex parte Davis\">317 U. S. 592</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"103796\"><a href=\"/opinion/103796/ex-parte-elmer-davis/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ex Parte Elmer Davis\">318 U. S. 412</a></span>; <em>Ex parte Williams, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"8157879\"><a href=\"/opinion/8195944/ex-parte-williams/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ex parte Williams\">317 U. S. 604</a></span>. Refusal of the writ, without more, is not an adjudication on the merits and is to be taken as without prejudice to an application to any other court for the relief sought.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}